'- R7: the finite-prime obstruction is extended to the rational criterion by controlling the field where the relevant p-torsion becomes rational. A bound depending only on p and g cannot be inferred from the small witnesses in examples.',
'- R8: setting the rational method aside was not a valid reason to discard the finite-field projector argument. That argument works over the exact pointed field. Arbitrary enlargement can destroy a p-unit condition; the simple Frobenius quotient gives a controlled enlargement that preserves it.',
'- R9: the dependent reconstruction chain is checked with arithmetic finite quotients retained and integral Tate-Hom used over a finitely generated descent field. Proper algebraic Galois extensions of finitely generated characteristic-zero fields, and finitely generated extensions of those, form a proved positive class. A separate normal-image proof establishes reconstruction for all finitely generated transcendental extensions of arbitrary characteristic-zero fields. The exact AP-F.37/F.43–F.49 subfield classes are restated with their normal-closure hypotheses; arbitrary subfield closure is not asserted.',
'- L1/A3 need a nontrivial cover: G=1 makes the numerical test vacuous and supplies no contradiction. For nontrivial odd constant G, the whole-relative criterion already reduces to a prime cyclic quotient. Nonconstant geometric deck groups do not enlarge its all-extension scope, although they can produce a witness over a smaller field.',
'- L2 is a point sum only in genus two. In general the exact formula uses rational effective divisors through degree 2g−2; modulo p it reduces through g−1. A change of Abel base point twists each coefficient by its degree.',
'- L3’s pair-count bound has the exact subtraction −N. Its genus-two singleton proof requires the primitive-root restriction. The displayed large-p inequality does not create the required quotient or prime and therefore does not decide a universal range of (p,g).',
'- The direct L5 rational-target proof kills one rational lifted difference and gives equality of divisor classes after norm; its effective-divisor step needs control of all translates, geometric p-rank zero, or the stated gonality condition. A1 now proves the unqualified collision-dependent implication, so that implication is no longer open. The exact finite spectral test includes the trivial character for the whole Jacobian and omits it only when testing the new part. In characteristic two an ordinary elliptic curve always has rational nonzero 2-torsion; it cannot be the suggested rationally 2-torsion-free target.',
'- L11 requires semilinear Frobenius and explicit base-point identifications. Freeness at every level is stronger than freeness on a selected cofinal subsystem because norm can destroy freeness. An arbitrary module vector has not been identified with a compatible family of differences of points.',
'', '# Manuscript readings', '',
'At cote 149, scan 35, the reduction through a finite-type model and a finite residue field is supported by the exact SGA specialization comparison. The doubtful word before “de type fini” does not affect the mathematical proof. At scan 36 the covering condition is exactly the full collision condition, not a stronger shortcut; the final implication is now proved by the full-group A1 argument. Its margin about Theoreme 2 is valid in the relative geometric prime-to-p convention established at scan 22.',
'',
'At scan 52, “au dessus de X_et” is treated as the stated base slip for S_et. The relative commutation 2-cell remains part of a morphism over the base; “pinned” separately means closed-point-preserving. Absolute Frobenius being isomorphic to identity as an absolute topos morphism does not erase the relative structural cell. The loop-structure wording is unnecessary for the number-field experiment once the full birational theorem is applied. At scans 6–8 the model pro-system is given a precise coherent relative meaning; no additional palaeographic certainty or automatic ordinary pro-category equivalence is claimed.',
'', '# Exact remaining work and failed steps', '',
'A3: neither counting, a fixed finite prime set, nor a nonabelian whole-relative cover supplies universal witnesses. The nonconstant-deck route reduces back to the same all-extension prime problem. The two ordinary geometric configurations (1,α,α) and its conjugate no longer obstruct the F4 rational census: mixed-character covers of degrees11 and113 give witnesses. Single-elliptic-factor covers are structurally excluded, and all primes3,5,7 are excluded for the final24 points. The retained fixed-field full Abel-pullback tower gives an alternative sufficient route to A1: a scalar annihilator works without rational decks because its geometric group needs more than two generators and cannot act freely on an elliptic curve. For D_n=C times_J J under multiplication by ell^n, the sufficient inequality is exp J_Dn(k)[p-infinity]−1<ell^(gn). The base Jacobian exponent is bounded over the first constant-deck fields, but no estimate has been proved for the new factors. Different-prime Iwasawa convergence results do not supply that missing bound. Universal A3 still lacks a theorem guaranteeing a successful mixed or geometric character for every curve. The scalar-Frobenius shortcut has been refuted by the exact degree13 example. The improved simultaneous counting theorem uses the much smaller subgroup ell J, rather than one character kernel, but still needs suitable prime factors. A proved scalar-primitive Frobenius obstruction identifies primes that fail over every extension. If p is primitive moduloell and rational ell-rank exceedsg, the Weil pairing forces ell−1 to divide the field exponent; this restricts the counting route and does not prove universal existence.',
'',
'A5/A6/A7: the universal nontrivial cyclic primitive-cover existence claim is now false. A direct explicit supersingular genus-two pencil, its degree-two Jacobian isogeny to E squared, and a scalar-Frobenius conductor cutoff n<10r^3 turn the generic torsion-incidence phenomenon into a finite-field existence proof. The simple proof works over F_(2^128); the original exact conductor and Jordan-totient count gave at least59,927,733,332 counterexample parameters over F_(2^38). The complete theta-packet refinement now leaves only191 and229 and improves this to274,515,649,064 parameters. More strongly, the parameter t defined by the irreducible polynomial Z^38+Z^14+Z^10+Z^9+Z^8+Z^5+Z^2+Z+1 gives an individually specified counterexample C: y^2+y=((u^2+t^2u+t)/(t^3+1))^3. Eight retained binary coefficient arrays certify two exact Bezout identities in F_(2^38)[u], proving that its theta curve has no nonzero191- or229-torsion. Independent bit-polynomial programs verify irreducibility and the torsion meaning of the division polynomials; the exact coefficients are independently reloaded and multiplied. All these curves satisfy A1 because their geometric two-primary Jacobian group is zero. For their distinguished Weierstrass point, the pointed hyperelliptic involution refines the scalar obstruction: every possible prime-cyclic rational witness has 19 dividing the multiplicative order of 2 modulo its prime, and therefore has prime at least191. This holds over every finite extension, without asserting that191 succeeds. If A6 allows degree one, the identity cover works on these curves; the positive-p-rank case of that literal variant remains undecided. Thus the finite-field counterexample does not rely on a countability shortcut, but its nontrivial-cover scope is essential. Existing nonordinariness theorems still do not force nilpotence in higher-dimensional character spaces. A nonabelian small-annihilator criterion only needs the actual finite rational p-primary group to have a small integral annihilator; in particular m>(p^e−1)^2 suffices when p^e is its exponent. No uniform bound of this kind is known from the arguments here, and constantizing a cover can enlarge that exponent. A nonabelian group-ring image could also be more flexible than a whole Prym, but a curve reached by that route and by no A3 witness over any extension has not been established.',
'',
'A4: the exhaustive F3 pointed plane-quartic computation and its proof are complete (3001 smooth pointed classes;2368 base-field witnesses;637 proved least prime5). Independent exact integer resultants reproduce every one of the2692 mod-three tests. The F5 pointed quartic census is also complete:94283 classes,134422 tests,89906 base-field witnesses,39917 proved least prime3. Its full integer resultant audit is complete and agrees with every direct coefficient and mod-five resultant/gcd check. Least primes outside the explicitly proved cases remain unknown; all tests actually tried are retained.',
'',
'A10: every original F4 pointed genus-two pair has no Frobenius-fixed vector free at every level because of its L1 witness, including 203/302. A1 now excludes all point-origin collision vectors. General genus-two nonexistence of arbitrary free vectors and a converse from those vectors to points are not proved. A semilinear simultaneous-projector theorem now treats all relative cyclic-prime tests over all constant extensions. Compactness constructs an actual nonzero two-torsion element in the full inverse limit when those hereditary tests all fail. Conversely a successful relative test with normal source and base kills a normal-level-free vector. A source that is not normal over the original curve cannot silently replace a normal level. The abstract countermodels are explicitly not asserted to come from curves.',
'',
'F3/F4: the centralizer condition controls invertible semilinear ghosts, while a general pinned map still requires Kummer integrality and actual-value descent. No proof of sufficiency follows from the known examples. The specified defect field Q(t,Σt^(n!))^h remains unresolved: fixing the second transcendental generator while sending t to t+t² fails to preserve its valuation. The Qbar-coefficient version is negative for a different, fully proved central-inertia reason. The countable transcendence-degree-zero test K_p=Frac(Z_(p)^sh) is now proved positive by the p-primary functional detector, arithmetic descent forced by actual values, an integral Picard1motive calculation, and a bounded resultant argument. Its normal closure over any number field inside it is the full algebraic closure, so the proper-normal theorem does not cover it. A connected good-reduction prime-to-p elliptic isogeny splits above every closed point overK_p, proving that the earlier Hilbertian finite-quotient detector fails there. The p-primary functional-detection route has been proved and independently reviewed. It replaces the failed finite-quotient detector and yields reconstruction for every algebraic field overQ admitting a discrete mixed-characteristic valuation. The tame extension T_p and every finite extension are also proved positive, as are all finite-transcendence-degree subfields of Qpbar with bounded p-primary ramification. For U_p=T_p(mu_{p-infinity}), every finite extension has trivial centralizer in Aut(Qbar); nevertheless an explicit CM elliptic curve over U5 gives a nonzero functional invisible to all point Kummer classes. This is a failure of that detector, not a reconstruction counterexample. The detected/invisible decomposition is now proved using Hodge–Tate comparison and the exact Sen inertia theorem. Actual values force arithmetic descent of the detected part; finite-local restriction recovers rational boundary residues; the resultant and scalar arguments recover the complete point function. This proves reconstruction for U_p, its finite extensions and all their subfields. The invisible-quotient method also proves reconstruction for K_p^ab and all fixed finite-class nilpotent stages K_{p,c}, their finite extensions and their subfields. Abelian or nilpotent inertia has potentially semisimple Hodge–Tate action, and the nilpotent one-dimensional cocycle obstruction vanishes. Every stage extension is infinite. No passage to an unbounded union, a general solvable closure, or centralizer sufficiency has been proved. The maximal metabelian extension B_p of K_p is now an explicit countable transcendence-degree-zero remaining test: every finite extension meets the centralizer condition, while all elements of K_p^ab become infinitely p-divisible in B_p. Its reconstruction status remains open. The actual elliptic curve y²+xy=x³−p now gives an exact nonsplit Hodge–Tate example: the quotient by all-point-invisible functionals has an invariant vector, but that vector has no inertia-invariant lift over any finite local extension. This refutes the invariant-lift step over B_p. The proof uses actual global algebraic points obtained by local approximation, not an unsupported claim that a Tate analytic uniformizer is globally algebraic. Symbolic integral identities verify the curve invariants and the free-wild-group commutator certificate. Neither failure produces a pinned topos ghost. The exact p-Kummer kernel over every finite E/B_p is now determined: it is the radical closure W of K_p^ab inside B_p, independent of E. The equation W intersect (1−W)=K_p^ab minus {0,1} recovers that subfield. All rational target translates detect values outside it; a further finite base change and two translated punctures detect every geometric value. This proves an exact uniqueness criterion for point functions under explicit equality of the pulled-back classes, but does not manufacture the arithmetic comparison or the needed compatible classes.',
'',
'F1(iii)/F6: the coherent relative levelwise model theorem is proved, but model transitions themselves need not preserve closed points. A bare commuting square after transcendental scalar extension is not a descent datum. The full class of morphisms in an unspecified ordinary pro-category has not been identified with the coherent model category.',
'',
'Further fixed-tower audits: a fixed integral Frobenius cocycle A(X)=1−2X has return valuation 3^(n−1) at primitive 3^n-th roots, so bounded polynomial degree and bounded two-part of the period do not bound that valuation. A fixed rank-one overconvergent unit-root isocrystal would give a bound, but the genuine cubic and order13 fibers of the specified genus-two curve cannot lie in one such rank-one interpolation over a common geometrically connected base. A separate fixed ordinary elliptic family E_a:y²+xy=x³+a has parameters of every positive odd degree m with rational group Z/(2^(2m)) and unit-root return valuation2m. This family has genuine geometric origin and weight one. An additional proof now places the divergence in the single fixed3-power parameter sequence: at primitive3^n-th roots the valuation tends to infinity. It extends every finite frame torsor of the étale two-divisible quotient across the split multiplicative cusp, then uses Artin–Schreier–Witt monomial expansions and exact cyclotomic trace cancellation. No rate of divergence is established, and this family has not been realized inside the fixed Abel tower. The needed bound on that tower remains an exact open input.',
'',
'For every finite E/B_p, each pinned automorphism of the affine-line étale topos now has an actual geometric point function x↦ux+v with u in E× and v in E. The proof uses the two-puncture Kummer detector, affine geometry over K_p^ab, and the trivial absolute-Galois centralizer. It does not yet identify the entire topos automorphism, and it treats automorphisms rather than arbitrary pinned maps. Carlson–Haine–Wolf Proposition4.14 requires compatible actual maps on every quasicompact separated étale object; the affine-line point function alone does not meet that hypothesis. Generic restriction is now proved faithful on the pointwise kernel of pinned automorphisms of a smooth characteristic-zero curve. The remaining kernel injects into the relative birational outer automorphism group fixing each finite-point inertia class and its residue action. A generic inner action cannot hide an extra topos automorphism. A converse site construction now extends a generic action that preserves the specified geometric inertia classes. Applying it to cyclic rational covers proves that the remaining generic action is trivial on every abelian profinite quotient after every finite constant extension. The genus-zero portion of the covering category is also fixed naturally; an exact S3 degree-three cover excludes the displayed full-profinite partial-conjugation example. This does not exclude every lift of its pro-p image. The natural realization now extends through finite products, opens, Galois closures and finite group quotients. This proves rigidity on all abelian covers of the line, of arbitrary genus, all Galois covers with genus-one source, and every degree-three genus-one cover, including non-Galois covers. The last assertion has a complete finite S4-to-S3 lifting certificate: all19375 candidate tuples were exhausted,582 survived the genus-one/product/generation conditions, and every one has exactly12 suitable lifts. An independent root program uses conjugation on the three nonidentity Klein-four elements and reproduces the entire certificate. The fixed-genus composition-factor theorem shows that this generated category is not cofinal among all covers; that fact does not produce a nontrivial automorphism kernel. A further integral averaging argument now proves identity on every Kummer character of every realized genus-one Galois slice, after every finite constant extension. The proof first repairs a genuine boundary issue: sufficiently many conjugate genus-zero Lattes quotients separate every completed geometric point, including omitted ramification points. Multiplication by n and its n^2 translations then give n b(f)=n^2 b_n(h) in integral geometric H1; divisibility for every n kills the possible unramified error. Corestriction and the rational-base norm identity kill the residual constant character without choosing a rational point. This fixes cyclic generic covering objects, not their actual point functions, the nonabelian generic action, or arbitrary pinned morphisms. The remaining birational stabilizer and noninvertible-map questions stay open.',
'' ,
'A further A1 route has been audited at the full group level. For a complex proper curve C of genus at least two, a cyclic triple cover of C and the full mod-three homology cover construct a nonisotrivial Kodaira fibration whose punctured total space has three-group Galois closure over Conf2(C). If the whole pro-odd configuration fiber map were injective, the actual compact-fiber monodromy would have odd image modulo every odd prime. Feit–Thompson and the field-independent solvable-length theorem force the integral monodromy to be solvable; Deligne Hodge II Corollary4.2.9(a) and the period map then force isotriviality, a contradiction. SGA1 XIII2.9–2.10 transports the fiber-inclusion diagram to characteristic two. The explicit model y²+y=x⁵ overZ2 supplies a completely specified genus-two example. The proof is existential at the profinite-kernel level: no nonidentity kernel element or particular finite monodromy matrix is claimed to have been enumerated. Numerical family invariants are checked by an exact program. The root and both other research agents independently audited the comparison. Strong approximation extends the obstruction to every prime p: after a finite-index rational lift through the simply connected central covering, Nori Theorem5.4 gives full congruence images outside finitely many primes. Completely split primes congruent to1 modulo arbitrarily large powers of p supply a split torus whose p-part survives the bounded central kernel. The original homology images therefore cannot all have order prime to p. This refutes the sufficient left-exactness question in Saidi–Tamagawa2009 Remark3.13 for every p; it neither refutes nor proves A1. A separate exact calculation shows why naive cuspidal induction fails: compactifying a degree-nine cover inside a cuspidally pro-three quotient retains only8 dimensions of H1 modulo an odd prime different from3, while its actual genus-thirteen compactification has26. The discarded18 dimensions cannot be restored by taking that open subgroup and killing puncture inertia. This is a failure of that procedure, not a proof that every combined cuspidal method fails. The exact sequence retaining the full tame base and completing only the relative kernel, as in Hoshi–Sawada–Tsujimura2024, has different data and does not repair this route. Single-prime pro-ell exactness is also compatible with the obstruction. Conversely, every visible open subgroup in a maximal cuspidally pro-r quotient retains its full pro-r completion: a finite-quotient core argument makes the cuspidal image an r-by-r group, so it kills exactly the original kernel. Compactification therefore retains full same-prime H1 and the exact Frobenius Weil polynomial. The retention lemma alone does not prove point separation. Those visible covers can be ramified at the puncture, so R1 cannot simply provide lifted point differences on them. The completed proof instead uses all their point counts to recognize actual noncuspidal sections, and then a cuspidal central difference cocycle and integral Kummer evaluations. The fixed-prime boundary construction supplies the required exceptional-coordinate comparison independently of the disputed full configuration assertion.',
'A late source audit located a concrete convention conflict, which the accepted proof avoids through an independent fixed-prime construction. Mochizuki’s June2007 author PDF, Proposition1.8(ii) (Proposition1.6(ii) in its LaTeX version), identifies a punctured fiber group with the inverse image of a point decomposition group in the configuration group. Under the displayed full pro-Sigma convention with Sigma=prime-to-p, this conflicts with the independently proved configuration obstruction above. The February2014 comments do not change that assertion. In Saidi–Tamagawa2009, Corollary2.3 constructs its named cuspidal comparison only for punctures outside the exceptional set, whereas Theorem2.7 invokes that comparison in a more broadly worded statement. No exceptional-point reconstruction theorem is taken from those statements without resolving the scope. The conditional point-recognition and Kummer-evaluation steps subsequently passed a separate full proof audit. The new fixed-prime fiber and boundary comparisons supply their hypotheses, so A1 is now PROVED. The primary SGA1 XIII5.2 Kummer-chart statement and the free-pro-r center-free input were opened directly; the audit is retained in notes/A1_full_chain_root_audit.md.',
'', '# Typesetting and reproducibility', '',
'The paper is assembled as one self-contained TeX source by code/assemble_paper.py. Original contributions are retained with a statement-number map, and the CSV has one row for every current numbered statement. code/build_latex.py records LuaLaTeX and BibTeX passes in qa/. The container initially lacked its generated LuaLaTeX format and the optional OpenType font loader; the build uses installed Type 1 Latin Modern fonts and records the dependency repair. The first successful PDF had one overfull box exceeding2pt, of54.38254pt; moving its long field coefficient to a display removed it. The next76-page build had zero overfull boxes of any size, no undefined citations or references, and nine rendered pages were inspected, including the former overflow page26. Visual review also caught claim references inheriting subsection numbers; explicit claim labels repair that error. The85-page checkpoint02 build again had zero warnings and zero overfull boxes; its rendered pages26,50,85 were inspected and are clean. The expanded115-page build likewise has zero warnings and zero overfull boxes; thirteen pages were rendered and pages62,100,109 were inspected and are clean. That build had115 unique mapped claims; the checkpoint03 build has125 pages and121 claims, with no warnings, overfull boxes or unresolved references after the final additions. qa/layout_history.json, qa/checkpoint02_build_check.json and qa/current_build_check.json retain these records; The checkpoint04 build has151 pages and138 numbered claims (A95,F43), with zero LuaLaTeX warnings, zero overfull boxes and no unresolved citations or references. It has55 bibliography entries, each with a verification marker. Thirteen pages were rendered and pages1,45,74,90,110,141,143,145,151 were visually inspected and are clean. The reproducibility inventory lists72 retained program sources. qa/checkpoint04_build_check.json and its render record retain the exact checks; The fifth-hour build has160 pages and143 numbered claims (A98,F45), zero warnings and zero overfull boxes, no unresolved references,61 marked bibliography entries, and77 canonical program sources at that build. Eleven pages were rendered; pages1,46,75,112,151,155,160 were visually inspected and are clean. qa/fifth_hour_build_check.json and qa/fifth_hour_render_record.json record these checks. Later builds will refresh the final counts.',
